class Solution {
    public int[][] intervalIntersection(int[][] firstList, int[][] secondList) {

        ArrayList<int[]> res = new ArrayList<>();

        int i = 0;
        int j = 0;

        while (i < firstList.length && j < secondList.length) {

            int start1 = firstList[i][0];
            int end1 = firstList[i][1];

            int start2 = secondList[j][0];
            int end2 = secondList[j][1];

            // Find intersection
            int start = Math.max(start1, start2);
            int end = Math.min(end1, end2);

            // If intersection exists
            if (start <= end) {
                res.add(new int[]{start, end});
            }

            // Move the interval which ends first
            if (end1 <= end2) {
                i++;
            } else {
                j++;
            }
        }

        return res.toArray(new int[res.size()][]);
    }
}


/*res naam ki ArrayList banao jisme intersections store karenge.
Do pointers lo:
i = 0 → firstList ke liye
j = 0 → secondList ke liye
Jab tak dono lists khatam nahi hoti:
Current intervals lo:
firstList[i] = [start1, end1]
secondList[j] = [start2, end2]
Current dono intervals ka intersection find karo:
start = max(start1, start2)
end = min(end1, end2)
Agar start <= end hai:
Dono intervals overlap kar rahe hain.
[start, end] ko res mein add karo.
Ab decide karo kaunsa pointer move karna hai:
Agar end1 <= end2 → i++
Else → j++
Reason: jis interval ka end chhota hai, woh future intervals ke saath intersection nahi bana sakta, isliye usko aage move kar do.
Jab i == firstList.length ya j == secondList.length ho jaye:
Loop stop karo.
Finally res ko int[][] mein convert karke return karo.
*/